           <figcaption> <h3>fig capture: forest soil</h3></figcaption>
            </figure>
            <br>

            <b>✅ Forest and Mountain Soil</b>
            <p>
                Forest and mountain soil is found in hilly and mountainous regions.
                It is formed by the decomposition of forest leaves and organic materials.
            </p>

            <br>

            <b>📍 Where is it Found in India?</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Himalayan region</li>
                <li>Jammu & Kashmir</li>
                <li>Himachal Pradesh</li>
                <li>Uttarakhand</li>
                <li>North-Eastern states</li>
            </ul>

            <br>

            <b>🎨 Colour and Nature</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Usually dark brown</li>
                <li>Rich in organic matter</li>
                <li>Fertility depends on altitude and climate</li>
            </ul>

            <br>

            <b>🌧️ Formation</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Formed by falling leaves and forest waste</li>
                <li>Rainfall and cold climate help soil formation</li>
            </ul>

            <br>

            <b>🌾 Crops Grown</b>
            <p>
                ✔ Tea <br>
                ✔ Coffee <br>
                ✔ Spices <br>
                ✔ Fruits (Apple, Peach, etc.)
            </p>

            <br>

            <b>⚠️ Limitations</b>
            <ul>
                <li>Soil erosion is common in hilly areas</li>
                <li>Fertility varies from place to place</li>
            </ul>

        </section>

    </div>

</div>

